BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prototype-fund-switzerland-responsible-sustainable-ai-2026-27@artificia
 lnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T130244Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: Prototype Fund Switzerland 2026-27: Responsible and Susta
 inable AI
DESCRIPTION:Since 2020 the Prototype Fund Switzerland has strengthened the 
 common good with open-source\, public-interest technology\, supporting int
 erdisciplinary teams to develop and test early-stage projects that show ho
 w open source\, data and digital technologies such as AI can create real s
 ocietal value. The 2026-2027 edition focuses on Responsible and Sustainabl
 e AI: building the path toward a more responsible and sustainable AI\, tec
 h and digitalization landscape\, open source and beyond. THIS YEAR'S FOCUS
 : projects that reduce resource use\, energy consumption or emissions\; st
 rengthen accountability\, transparency and governance\; and contribute to 
 resilient and trustworthy digital systems\, including sustainable digitali
 zation and digital sufficiency\, public-interest AI and data infrastructur
 es\, and tools for governance\, oversight or digital sovereignty. PUBLIC I
 NTEREST TECH areas span sustainability and climate\, participation and civ
 ic tech\, education and literacy\, health and inclusion\, and open knowled
 ge and data. WHO THEY FUND: individuals and small teams open to open sourc
 e\, AI and iterative experimentation\, eager to combine technical capabili
 ty with societal and political awareness\, willing to share learnings\, mo
 tivated to work on pressing societal problems through technology\, with an
  early-stage but well-thought-out concept\, and eligible to work in Switze
 rland. SUPPORT: up to CHF 50\,000 in funding\, a 4-month prototyping phase
 \, coaching\, mentoring and workshops\, and access to a strong network acr
 oss tech\, policy and society. Teams are strongly encouraged (though not r
 equired) to publish code\, data or components under open-source licenses a
 nd to document their approach. TIMELINE: applications 21 July to 7 Septemb
 er 2026\; rolling jury selection August-September 2026\; prototyping mid-O
 ctober 2026 to mid-February 2027\; outputs and learnings November 2026 to 
 July 2027. Questions: info@prototypefund.ch.\n\nOrganisation: Prototype Fu
 nd Switzerland (Opendata.ch)\nLocation: Switzerland\; applicants must be e
 ligible to work in Switzerland.\nAward: Up to CHF 50\,000 per project\, pl
 us coaching\, mentoring and workshops and access to a tech/policy/society 
 network. No application fee.\nDuration: 4-month prototyping phase (mid-Oct
 ober 2026 to mid-February 2027)\n\nMore: https://prototypefund.opendata.ch
 /en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prototypefund.opendata.ch/en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland\; applicants must be eligible to work in Switzerland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stichting-stokroos-residency-fundaziun-nairs-2026@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T130244Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260911
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260912
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Stokroos: Residency at Fundaziun Nairs 2026
DESCRIPTION:Stichting Stokroos funds a three-month reflective residency at 
 Fundaziun Nairs in Scuol\, Switzerland\, for one selected visual artist\, 
 designer or craft practitioner (overlap possible). Both emerging and estab
 lished makers may apply. Stokroos covers full accommodation and meals dire
 ctly with Fundaziun Nairs and provides a discretionary EUR 7\,000 budget f
 or living\, travel and production. The application should include a propos
 al that engages specifically with the residency\, its Alpine surroundings 
 and/or its historical and cultural context. Eligibility: you completed you
 r first subject-specific (vocational or higher) programme in 2022 or earli
 er\, or have an equivalent established practice\, or started without forma
 l training (first presentation marks the start of your practice)\; at leas
 t 21 years old\; living and working in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (inc
 luding its Caribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; not curren
 tly enrolled in a study or post-academic programme. Applications are indiv
 idual only\; duos and collectives cannot apply. Makers already selected by
  Fundaziun Nairs may still apply if they meet the criteria. You may submit
  only one application per year across all Stokroos grants\, and must not h
 ave received a Seed Grant rejection in the previous calendar year. Apply v
 ia the online form (Dutch or English) with a portfolio PDF up to 20 pages\
 , optional video up to 10 minutes total\, CV up to 2 pages\, and work/plan
  descriptions up to 2\,500 characters each. Selection includes an introduc
 tory interview with up to three candidates\; Stokroos aims to respond with
 in 8 weeks. No appeal is possible. Application window: 1 to 11 September 2
 026. More information at nairs.ch.\n\nOrganisation: Stichting Stokroos\nLo
 cation: Residency in Scuol\, Switzerland (Fundaziun Nairs). Applicants mus
 t live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean
  parts) or Suriname for at least one year. Applicants outside the Randstad
  particularly encouraged.\nAward: Fully supported stay (accommodation and 
 meals paid directly to Fundaziun Nairs) plus an unrestricted living\, trav
 el and production budget of EUR 7\,000. 80% paid before the residency\, th
 e remainder on receipt of a brief final report. No application fee.\nDurat
 ion: Intensive three-month working period (July through September).\n\nMor
 e: https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/guidelines-residency-fundaziun-nairs
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/guidelines-residency-fundaziun-nairs
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency in Scuol\, Switzerland (Fundaziun Nairs). Applicants mus
 t live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Caribbean
  parts) or Suriname for at least one year. Applicants outside the Randstad
  particularly encouraged.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-game-design-pre-production-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T130244Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270301
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270302
SUMMARY:Deadline: Game Design Emerging Talents: Pre-Production
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's Game Design Emerging Talents pre-production gran
 t supports early-career game designers in developing playable prototypes f
 or digital games. Emerging Talents are game developers or studios whose ga
 me-design education or company foundation dates back less than seven years
 . ELIGIBILITY: requires a connection to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, o
 r permanent residency with regular artistic activity in Switzerland)\; not
  open to practitioners without a Swiss connection. At least 50 percent of 
 participants must be Swiss citizens or permanent residents whose place of 
 work is in Switzerland. AMOUNT: up to CHF 20\,000\, plus possible addition
 al coaching. Deadlines twice a year: 1 March (23:59 CET) and 1 September (
 23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia portal.\n\nOrganisation: Pro Helve
 tia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Switzerland-based emerging game design
 ers and studios.\nAward: Up to CHF 20\,000\, plus possible additional coac
 hing. No application fee.\nDuration: Pre-production / prototype phase\; de
 adlines twice yearly (1 March and 1 September)\; next window opens 1 Janua
 ry 2027 for the 1 March 2027 deadline.\n\nMore: https://prohelvetia.ch/en/
 find-support/game-design-emerging-talents-pre-production?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/game-design-emerging-talents-pre
 -production?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland-based emerging game designers and studios.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-game-design-production-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T130244Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270301
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270302
SUMMARY:Deadline: Game Design Emerging Talents: Production
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's Game Design Emerging Talents production grant fu
 nds the production of digital games based on advanced prototypes or vertic
 al slices. Emerging Talents are studios whose game-design education or com
 pany foundation dates back less than seven years. Applicants must be legal
  entities (sole proprietorships accepted if willing to convert). ELIGIBILI
 TY: requires a connection to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, or permanent
  residency with regular artistic activity in Switzerland)\; not open to pr
 actitioners without a Swiss connection. At least 50 percent of participant
 s must be Swiss citizens or permanent residents whose place of work is in 
 Switzerland. AMOUNT: up to CHF 50\,000\, requiring a matching grant of equ
 al value from own or third-party funding. Deadlines twice a year: 1 March 
 (23:59 CET) and 1 September (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia porta
 l.\n\nOrganisation: Pro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Switzerla
 nd-based emerging game studios.\nAward: Up to CHF 50\,000\, requiring a ma
 tching grant of equal value from own or third-party funding. No applicatio
 n fee.\nDuration: Production phase\; deadlines twice yearly (1 March and 1
  September)\; next window opens 1 January 2027 for the 1 March 2027 deadli
 ne.\n\nMore: https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/game-design-emerging-t
 alents-production?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/game-design-emerging-talents-pro
 duction?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland-based emerging game studios.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-game-design-post-production-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261102T130244Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270301
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270302
SUMMARY:Deadline: Game Design Emerging Talents: Post-Production
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's Game Design Emerging Talents post-production gra
 nt funds the dissemination and marketing of advanced game-design projects.
  Emerging Talents are studios whose game-design education or company found
 ation dates back less than seven years. Applicants must be legal entities 
 (sole proprietorships accepted if willing to convert). ELIGIBILITY: requir
 es a connection to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, or permanent residency
  with regular artistic activity in Switzerland)\; not open to practitioner
 s without a Swiss connection. At least 50 percent of participants must be 
 Swiss citizens or permanent residents whose place of work is in Switzerlan
 d. AMOUNT: up to CHF 20\,000\, plus potential individual coaching. Deadlin
 es twice a year: 1 March (23:59 CET) and 1 September (23:59 CEST). Apply v
 ia the Pro Helvetia portal.\n\nOrganisation: Pro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Coun
 cil)\nLocation: Switzerland-based emerging game studios.\nAward: Up to CHF
  20\,000\, plus potential individual coaching. No application fee.\nDurati
 on: Post-production\, dissemination and marketing phase\; deadlines twice 
 yearly (1 March and 1 September)\; next window opens 1 January 2027 for th
 e 1 March 2027 deadline.\n\nMore: https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/g
 ame-design-emerging-talents-post-production?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/game-design-emerging-talents-pos
 t-production?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland-based emerging game studios.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-she-got-game-switzerland-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T130244Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Game Design Emerging Talents: She Got Game (Switzerland)
DESCRIPTION:She Got Game is a Pro Helvetia mentoring programme promoting eq
 ual opportunities for women in the Swiss and international game industry\,
  supporting the representation of women in management positions through di
 alogue with experienced international experts. This is the variant for pro
 fessional game designers FROM Switzerland who identify as women (a separat
 e variant exists for practitioners in the liaison-office regions). Emergin
 g Talents are developers or studios whose relevant training or registratio
 n dates back less than seven years. ELIGIBILITY: requires a connection to 
 Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, or permanent residency with regular artis
 tic activity in Switzerland)\; not open to practitioners without a Swiss c
 onnection. WHAT IS OFFERED: individual coaching on project development\, b
 usiness strategy\, finances\, marketing\, PR\, and pitch training\; a grow
 ing community of female game developers\; potential access to internationa
 l trade fairs\; CHF 3\,000 toward a prototype or demo\; and up to CHF 250 
 per week toward childcare or children's travel when attending trade fairs.
  Roughly 30 hours over six months. Submission deadline 1 September 2026 (2
 3:59 CEST)\; notification November 2026. Apply via the Pro Helvetia portal
 .\n\nOrganisation: Pro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Profession
 al game designers from Switzerland who identify as women.\nAward: CHF 3\,0
 00 toward prototype/demo production\, plus mentoring\, community access\, 
 and potential trade-fair access\; up to CHF 250 per week childcare support
  for international events. No application fee.\nDuration: Six-month mentor
 ing programme (approximately 30 hours total)\; notification November 2027.
  Next application window 1 July to 1 September 2027.\n\nMore: https://proh
 elvetia.ch/en/find-support/game-design-emerging-talents-she-got-game?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/game-design-emerging-talents-she
 -got-game?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Professional game designers from Switzerland who identify as women
 .
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eofa-artistic-research-residency-geneva-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261102T130244Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Embassy of Foreign Artists: Artistic Research Residency i
 n International Organisation Archives (Geneva\, 2027)
DESCRIPTION:The Embassy of Foreign Artists\, in partnership with the Centre
  for Digital Humanities and Multilateralism at the Geneva Graduate Institu
 te\, invites artists worldwide to a three-month artistic research residenc
 y in Geneva during 2027. The programme centres on archival research in the
  archives of Geneva-based international intergovernmental and non-governme
 ntal organisations (UN\, Red Cross and others): uncovering untold stories\
 , examining international decision-making\, reflecting on multilateral suc
 cesses and failures\, and imagining new possibilities for international co
 operation. Selected artists receive a CHF 1\,400 monthly residency grant\,
  accommodation in a private room with shared common areas\, artistic guida
 nce from EOFA\, connections with archive personnel\, and access to partici
 pating archives as primary research resource\; travel and production costs
  are the artist's own. ELIGIBILITY: professional artistic practice with a 
 demonstrable body of work (creations\, publications and/or performances)\,
  over 28 years old\, fluent in French or English\, not enrolled in basic a
 rt training\; individuals\, duos or groups may apply (same stipend). APPLY
  via the online form plus a single PDF (cover letter\, project description
 \, portfolio\, CV) emailed to application@eofa.ch. No application fee. Dea
 dline: 15 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Embassy of Foreign Artists / Ce
 ntre for Digital Humanities and Multilateralism\, Geneva Graduate Institut
 e\nLocation: Geneva\, Switzerland\nAward: CHF 1\,400 monthly residency gra
 nt plus accommodation in a private room\; travel and artistic production c
 osts are not covered\nDuration: 3 months\, during 2027\n\nMore: https://ww
 w.eofa.ch/en/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.eofa.ch/en/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Geneva\, Switzerland
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:schlossmediale-werdenberg-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T130244Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
SUMMARY:Deadline: Schlossmediale Call for Art Residency 2027 (Schloss Werde
 nberg\, Switzerland)
DESCRIPTION:Schlossmediale\, the international festival of early music\, ne
 w music and audiovisual art at Werdenberg Castle in the canton of St. Gall
 en\, invites three solo artists to a five-week residency from 17 May to 27
  June 2027. The works developed on site are shown in the castle during the
  14th festival edition (17-26 June 2027). The 2027 theme is KLATSCH! (Rumo
 ur-Impact): sound and rumour\, applause and gossip\, oral tradition\, coll
 ective memory\, and the ways every era spreads its information. MEDIUMS: s
 ound art\, sound studies\, audiovisual art\, experimental instrument build
 ing\, visual art\, installation\, sculpture\, land art and performance\; s
 ound installations without a visual dimension are not considered. SUPPORT:
  CHF 4\,000 grant\, CHF 1\,000 for travel\, transport and meals\, up to CH
 F 1\,000 for materials\, and accommodation in a shared house in Werdenberg
  (individual rooms\, shared kitchen and living areas). ELIGIBILITY: solo a
 rtists with professional experience (no groups or duos) who can live and w
 ork on site for the full period and complete a finished\, functional work 
 by the festival opening\; residents present their work on castle tours and
  attend the whole festival. Working space at the castle is limited and no 
 studios are provided. HOW TO APPLY: exclusively online via the application
  portal linked from the open-call page. DEADLINE: 18 October 2026.\n\nOrga
 nisation: Schlossmediale Werdenberg\nLocation: Werdenberg Castle\, canton 
 of St. Gallen\, Switzerland. Open internationally to solo artists\; accomm
 odation in a shared house in Werdenberg.\nAward: CHF 4\,000 grant per resi
 dent\, plus CHF 1\,000 for travel\, transport and meals\, up to CHF 1\,000
  for material costs\, and accommodation in a shared house (individual room
 s). Three residencies awarded.\nDuration: Five-week residency from 17 May 
 to 27 June 2027\, with the 14th Schlossmediale festival on 17-26 June 2027
 \n\nMore: https://schlossmediale.ch/festival-schlossmediale/ausstellung/op
 en-call-2027-en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://schlossmediale.ch/festival-schlossmediale/ausstellung/open-call
 -2027-en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Werdenberg Castle\, canton of St. Gallen\, Switzerland. Open inter
 nationally to solo artists\; accommodation in a shared house in Werdenberg
 .
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eth-ai-center-fellowships-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261102T130244Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:Deadline: ETH AI Center Doctoral and Postdoctoral Fellowships 2027
DESCRIPTION:The ETH AI Center's flagship fellowship programme funds doctora
 l and postdoctoral researchers doing interdisciplinary AI research\, eithe
 r within AI foundations or between AI foundations and application areas\, 
 including safe and trustworthy AI. Fellows are co-supervised across ETH gr
 oups and join the AI Center's community. ELIGIBILITY: doctoral track needs
  a Master's in computer science\, machine learning\, statistics\, physics\
 , engineering\, applied mathematics or a related field\, completed by June
  2027\; postdoc track needs a PhD completed by June 2027. Two to three ref
 erence letters are required. Selection weighs research excellence\, interd
 isciplinary collaboration and impact orientation. APPLICATION: separate po
 rtals for the doctoral and postdoc tracks (linked from the programme page)
 \; deadline 27 October 2026 at 16:00 CET. Related CLS and ELLIS PhD tracks
  have their own applications.\n\nOrganisation: ETH AI Center\, ETH Zurich\
 nLocation: Zurich\, Switzerland. In person at ETH Zurich.\nAward: Doctoral
  fellowship: CHF 73\,100 (year 1)\, CHF 78\,300 (year 2)\, CHF 83\,500 (ye
 ar 3). Postdoc fellowship: CHF 92\,500 (year 1)\, CHF 97\,200 (year 2). No
  application fee.\nDuration: About 3 years (doctoral\, extendable by up to
  1 year) or 2 years (postdoc)\, starting around September 2027.\n\nMore: h
 ttps://ai.ethz.ch/research/phd-and-postdoc-programs.html?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ai.ethz.ch/research/phd-and-postdoc-programs.html?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Zurich\, Switzerland. In person at ETH Zurich.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:traces-art-science-energypolis-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261102T130244Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: TRACES Art & Science @ Energypolis 2027: residency at the
  EPFL Laboratory for Energy Materials (Sion)
DESCRIPTION:TRACES is a new art and science residency run by the Foundation
  for the Sustainable Development of Mountain Regions (FDDM) with EPFL Vala
 is-Wallis\, Energypolis\, the City of Sion and the Canton of Valais. The 2
 027 pilot embeds one visual artist for three months in Prof. Sascha Feldma
 nn's Laboratory for Energy Materials at EPFL\, which works on light-matter
  interactions and soft semiconductors for flexible solar cells\, energy-ef
 ficient screens and emerging quantum technologies. The artist develops ori
 ginal work in dialogue with the lab around the energy transition and the m
 aterials of the future\, with studio and production space\, scientific men
 toring and a public final presentation on 15 April 2027. ELIGIBILITY: conf
 irmed\, professional international visual artists aged 25 or over who fini
 shed their studies at least two years ago and have at least two years of p
 rofessional practice\; applications in English or French with a letter of 
 intent (two A4 pages)\, portfolio and CV via the online form. Laureate sel
 ected 7 December 2026. DEADLINE: 22 November 2026\, 23:59 Swiss time (CET)
 .\n\nOrganisation: Foundation for the Sustainable Development of Mountain 
 Regions (FDDM) with EPFL Valais-Wallis\nLocation: Energypolis campus\, Sio
 n\, Valais\, Switzerland. In person.\nAward: Artist stipend of CHF 2\,000 
 per month (CHF 6\,000 total) covering living and research costs\, housing 
 in Sion\, travel from home and back up to CHF 1\,500\, and a separate prod
 uction budget set by the curator. No application fee.\nDuration: Three mon
 ths\, 11 January to 18 April 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.traces-opencall.ch
 /en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.traces-opencall.ch/en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Energypolis campus\, Sion\, Valais\, Switzerland. In person.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
